Subject: [PATCH 5/5] reasons: record which reasons fired on the object and which it inherited

APPLIES ON TOP OF 0004-successor-pointers.patch. Three files:

  es/EscapeReasons           an `own` side map; record() writes both maps, a new inherit() writes
                             only the union; own successor-pointer groups, interned.
  resolver/ReworkedResolver  collectReasons keeps, per member, what fired on that member;
                             stampComponent records those as own and the rest as inherited.
  main/Main                  printReasons writes two more columns, OWN and OWNGROUP.

WHY
---
resolve() escapes a whole resolver component when any member satisfies a condition, and
collectReasons mirrors it by stamping the component's reason union on every member
(Reason-Pipeline-Spec F-A5 / X-A4). The verdict needs that; the figures do not. A reason that fired
on one member is drawn as a reason of all of them, so a component of N members with k reasons
appears as N objects with k reasons each. On avrora under MarkStoreEscaping=false one component
holds 17,551 objects; 819 of 827 application objects carrying MONITOR have no monitorenter in
their method at all (Viz-Faithfulness-Audit 4.2).

The loop already knows which member each condition fired on. The union EnumSet threw that away.
This keeps it.

WHAT IS OWN
-----------
A reason is an object's own if it was recorded at a site that examined THAT object:
  * every handler site, the intraprocedural cascade, KillCallerOnly, stampReturned (all through
    record(), unchanged);
  * in collectReasons, the conditions evaluated on this member: RETURNED, NO_BCI_METHOD_AT_RESOLVER,
    ASSIGNED_TO_THIS_OR_PARAM, PARAM_ESCAPES_VIA_SUCCESSOR, TRANSITIVE_SUCCESSOR, and the reasons
    the member had already recorded itself before resolution reached it (getOwn, not get).
Everything else stampComponent puts on the member is inherited: EscapeReasons.inherit() adds it to
the union map and not to `own`. The union map, and so .reasons columns 1-4, are unchanged.

Own successor pointers are the successors this member's own propagated reasons fired through.
Unlike the component's union group they keep pointers to siblings, because a sibling that had
already escaped is a real cause for this member. They share viaGroups (one .via, one numbering);
identical sets are interned.

An own reason may still have reached the object intraprocedurally through a container
(recursiveCascadeEscape). This patch separates the resolver component only.

"INHERITED" IS NOT "WRONG"
--------------------------
An inherited reason is true for the verdict: Stava resolves the component jointly, and some
members escape only through the component. corpus/M02: `Item j` really escapes (b.item = j, then
publish(b)), but only through its component, so its reason is inherited. `Box a` never escapes in
the source and also carries only an inherited reason, through context-insensitive merging. The
split cannot tell those two apart; it says where the reason fired, not whether it is spurious.

OUTPUT
------
  .reasons  columns 6 and 7: OWN (comma list, a subset of column 4) and OWNGROUP (an index into
            .via, or empty). Columns 1-4 byte-identical to patch 0004. Column 5 names the same
            pointer set per object; its numbers can shift, because own groups take numbers in the
            same first-appearance sequence.

The extractor (extract/info_to_graph.py) returns the split as ReasonMap.own and joins it as
ownReasons / inheritedReasons. In roots mode an object's own propagated reasons resolve through
its own pointers; a pointer to a sibling resolves to the sibling's own direct reasons, not to the
component union, which would hand the union back as own.

WHAT IT DOES NOT CHANGE
-----------------------
No EscapeStatus is read that collectReasons did not already read; the union `fired` is computed
exactly as before. The check is tools/verify_patch5.sh (corpus, both configurations) and
tools/run_all_p5.sh (six benchmarks): .res line multiset identical to patch 0004, .reasons columns
1-4 identical, column-5 pointer sets identical, own within all on every line
(tools/compare_reasons_p4_p5.py). tools/own_witness.py checks the split against the bytecode.

